X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/especies-de-sonoma-ciencia-en-tu-celular/18508565/2026-04-07T17", "Press Democrat": "https://jacklondonpark.com/events/especiesdesonoma/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/especies-de-sonoma-ciencia-en-tu-celular/18508565/2026-04-07T17"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Especies de Sonoma: Ciencia en tu Celular
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260407T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260407T193000
UID:260405GOkGUq84T0yKNrPP4m1VXQ
DESCRIPTION:Sonoma County is incredibly rich in biodiversity: although it 
 covers only about 1% of California’s land area\, it is estimated to cont
 ain around 20% of the state’s biodiversity in a particularly diverse por
 tion of the Sonoma Valley.\n\nThis program\, presented in Spanish by Jack 
 London State Historic Park and the Sonoma Ecology Center\, will teach you 
 to use your phone to easily and enjoyably identify birds\, plants\, and an
 imals.\n\nThis program is designed as the first part of a three-part serie
 s focused on observing and identifying nature in Sonoma County:\n\nPart I.
  \\(July 4\, 2026\\) Join us at the Sonoma Valley Library for an interacti
 ve talk where you’ll learn how to use the Merlin Bird ID and iNaturalist
  apps\, two of the most popular and useful tools for identifying wildlife.
 \n\nPart II. \\(April 24\, 2026\\) Use what you learned in the library to 
 identify birds in Jack London State Historic Park with the help of Merlin 
 Bird ID.\n\nPart III. \\(April 25\, 2026\\) Use what you learned in the li
 brary to identify plants and animals in Sugarloaf Ridge State Park with th
 e help of iNaturalist.\n\nThis workshop will focus on:\n\nHow to use Merli
 n Bird ID to identify birds by song and photo\n\n• How to use iNaturalis
 t to identify and document plants\, birds\, insects\, and other animals\n\
 n• Basic tips for observing nature and improving your identification ski
 lls\n\n• General information about common birds\, plants\, and animals i
 n Sonoma Valley and Sonoma County\n\n• How these apps help scientists an
 d parks protect local biodiversity\n\nThis program\, presented in Spanish\
 , is ideal for beginners\, families\, nature lovers\, and anyone curious. 
 No prior experience is necessary. We will go step by step\, and there will
  be time for questions and guided practice.\n\nThis workshop will serve as
  preparation for guided walks on April 24 and 25 at Jack London State Hist
 oric Park and Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\, where we will put what we've le
 arned into practice in the field.\n\nFor more information\, contact Carlos
  Barragán at cbarragan@jacklondonpark.com or call 707-938-5216 ext. 9.
LOCATION:Sonoma Valley Library
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/especies-de-sonoma-cien
 cia-en-tu-celular/18508565/2026-04-07T17
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
