BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Press Democrat": "http://rclc.org/events"}
X-SOURCE-ID:pressdemocrat
SUMMARY:Giants of the Pacific: Gray Whales on the Mendonoma Coast
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260409T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260409T160000
UID:260324C1qNOrpDs0OlZDWzLISTyA
DESCRIPTION:Join Redwood Coast Land Conservancy at the stunning Sea Ranch 
 Lodge for an\n\nevening with renowned marine mammal researchers Scott and 
 Tree Mercer\,\n\nfounders of the Mendonoma Whale and Seal Study. In the Fi
 reside Lounge\, the\n\nMercers will share firsthand fieldwork\, population
  data\, behavioral observations\, and\n\ncompelling visuals about Pacific 
 gray whales along our coastline. After the talk\,\n\nguests are invited to
  explore the bluffs and look for gray whales themselves.\n\nScott Mercer h
 as been studying marine mammals since 1974\, founding New England\n\nWhale
  Watch in 1978 and co-authoring The Great Whale Book. A pioneer of\n\nwhal
 e-watching recognized by NOAA\, he brings 50 years of ocean observation to
  this\n\ntalk. Tree Mercer holds a Master's in Science Education and spent
  35 years teaching\n\nbiology and physics. Together\, the Mercers were fea
 tured in the Los Angeles Times\n\nand a UC Berkeley documentary for their 
 work on the gray whale Unusual Mortality\n\nEvent.\n\nA live jazz performa
 nce follows at 6:00 PM. The bar will be open for wine\, beer\,\n\ncocktail
 s\, and light bites. Admission is free\; dinner reservations are recommend
 ed.
LOCATION:The Sea Ranch Lodge
URL:http://rclc.org/events
X-SOURCE:Press Democrat
