X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Basketry: Weaving with Reclaimed Materials
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260409T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260409T200000
UID:260328eQ61smHpLkeou7HDXFq74A
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nThursday\, April 9\, 2026 5:30 PM – 8:00 PM\n\nL
 ocation\n\nRoom 201\, Fiber Arts Studio\n\nExperience Level\n\nBeginning\n
 \nEvent Categories: Fiber Arts\, Sustainability\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n14\\+\n\n
 Registration Cost:\n\n$40\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\nIncluded\n\nTotal Registrat
 ion Cost:\n\n$40\n\nWeave a funky basket from upcycled plastic\, fabric\, 
 wire and more. No experience needed.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nTurn everyday d
 iscards into funky\, functional art in this playful basketry workshop. Usi
 ng upcycled materials like plastic bags\, fabric strips\, caution tape\, a
 nd other unexpected finds\, you’ll learn how to weave a one-of-a-kind ba
 sket full of color and texture. No prior experience is needed. Leave with 
 a finished basket and fresh inspiration for transforming the overlooked in
 to something extraordinary.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/basketry-weaving-with-recla
 imed-materials/
