SUMMARY:Chris Pureka
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260410T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260410T000000
UID:260327ujL6pwVg90CuIwW6XkUahQ
DESCRIPTION:This is an intimate community center show at the Monan's Rill 
 Community Center in Santa Rosa. Doors are at 7pm and music starts at 8pm. 
 Suggested ticket is $35 but is sliding scale starting at $25. Please pay m
 ore if you can. All money goes directly to the artist and there are no tic
 ket fees. About Monan's Rill: The Rill is an intentional\, intergeneration
 al community in rural Sonoma County\, California. We hold a shared commitm
 ent to the land we live on\, to core community values\, and to one another
 .\n\nPlease pay close attention to the directions and parking info below. 
 Monan’s Rill is located at 7899 Saint Helena Road\, Santa Rosa 95404. On
 ce you turn off St Helena Rd at 7899 \\(big yellow mailbox\\) and get onto
  the gravel road\, please keep your speed below 15 mph. There will be a fe
 w forks in the road -- go LEFT at the first fork \\(sign for 7899\\). At t
 he second fork \\(entrance to Monan's Rill\\)\, those who have capacity to
  walk on variable terrain should take a LEFT at the second fork\, then rig
 ht at the "parking" sign for our large event parking area. Park in the mar
 ked areas\, then walk to the HUB \\(5 minute walk\\). For anyone who has a
 ccess needs\, take a right at the second fork instead\, and left at the th
 ird fork \\(follow signs for the HUB\\). There is more limited parking ava
 ilable directly adjacent to the HUB.
LOCATION:Monan's Rill Community Hub
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/108106137?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1037644550?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Mah Ze Tar x Elias Alexander x Mycelial
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260410T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260410T000000
UID:2603273w5Wx5aItkiGX1_sCMbQng
DESCRIPTION:ABOUT: \n\nMāh Ze Tār\n\nMāh Ze Tār is propelled by the vi
 sion of fusing traditional eastern music with modern electronic compositio
 n as a form of cultural preservation. Each Māh Ze Tār set is uniquely dy
 namic- The listener can expect to hear the ancient sounds of the Sitar and
  Oud in one song and the timeless melodies of the Hulusi\, Ney and Duduk i
 n the next- bringing a kaleidoscope of emotions through the wide plethora 
 of ancient sounds\, mesmerizing vocals\, and grooving beats. Māh Ze Tār 
 seeks to make familiar that which seems “other” through serving the so
 unds of distant lands on a platter of familiar body moving bass lines and 
 thumping grooves. Māh Ze Tār was an active performing member of Balkan B
 ump and has had significant musical collaborations with Desert Dwellers\, 
 David Starfire\, Jef Stott\, Morillo\, Akriza\, Nyrus and many others. Not
 able performances- Red Rocks\, Coachella\, Lightning in a Bottle\, Shambal
 a\, Gem & Jam\, Joshua Tree\, Lucidity\, Symbiosis\, Oregon Eclipse\, Burn
 ing Man\, Oregon Country Fair\, Haurkaze Tokyo Festival\n\nHuman Behind th
 e Project\n\nMaz Karandish is a Devotee of music- A well traveled vocalist
  & multi-instrumentalist covering grounds from Rāga\, Maqām\, and Dastg
 āh to Harmony\, Jazz\, and Opera. Maz feels deeply connected to the ancie
 nt musical traditions of the east that he began learning from a very young
  age. As an Ethnomusicologist and a practicing Psychologist\, he's come to
  recognize that people in his generation have an easier time engaging with
  traditional music when it’s integrated with familiar rhythmic and sonic
  environments- thus forming his vision of preserving cultural music throug
 h fusion-oriented avenues. Maz devotes his musical time to exploring the p
 ossible weaving of Indian\, Persian\, Greek and Turkish music with modern 
 soundscapes. He's currently most interested in the integration of Indian D
 hrupad and Persian Tahrir singing with electronic composition. Maz is an a
 ctive performing member of Balkan Bump\, has significant musical collabora
 tions with many electronic fusion artists. \n\nElias Alexander\n\nElias Al
 exander is a rare performer who combines live looping and electronics with
  a wide variety of instruments from bagpipes to fiddle\, guitar\, whistle 
 and keys. With deep roots in traditional Scottish and American music\, but
  a boundless appetite for possibility\, rhythm\, and expression\, Elias ta
 kes audiences on a mind blowing journey through traditional tunes\, origin
 al songs\, and danceable fun.\n\nProducer\, multi-instrumentalist\, and si
 nger Elias Alexander blends traditional Celtic sounds with EDM\, alchemizi
 ng original and ancient material\, live looping\, and driving beats into j
 ourneys of belonging\, connection\, and celebration.Having studied bagpipe
 s\, fiddle\, whistles\, and guitar from a young age\, Elias has found a wa
 y to weave his traditional music background into modern sounds\, creating 
 a blend that feels timeless\, crossing generations while remaining deeply 
 personal and authentic.\n\nSince emerging onto the scene in 2022\, Elias h
 as built a loyal following of over 115K humans across Instagram and Tik To
 k\, with viral videos that have captured millions of views and attention a
 round the globe\, leading to international tours and 29 festival appearanc
 es in 2025.Elias’s shows feel like a mixture of ritual and pure sillines
 s\, uniting the pure joy of dance music and the communal ritual of singing
  and moving together\, all built around his unique ability to connect with
  a crowd.\n\nMycelial\n\nRooted in tradition yet reaching toward the futur
 e\, Mycelial is the visionary electro-acoustic project of renowned banjois
 t Isaac Cantor. Emerging from the lush coastal forests of the West Coast\,
  Mycelial weaves together rootsy folk\, global influences\, and psychedeli
 c textures with deep electronic rhythms\, creating live performances that 
 are equal parts ritual\, dance party\, and hoe-down.\n\nWith four albums a
 nd multiple singles — including collaborations with Kr3ture\, Evan Frase
 r\, Evan Hatfield\, and Magdelion Moondrop — Mycelial is steadily growin
 g a dedicated audience across both streaming platforms and live stages. Ca
 ntor’s years of touring and recording with national acts such as the Gra
 teful Bluegrass Boys and Dusty Green Bones Band\, alongside performances w
 ith icons like Bob Weir \\(Grateful Dead\\)\, Billy Strings\, and members 
 of The String Cheese Incident\, ground his sound in deep musical lineage.\
 n\nNow\, as Mycelial\, Cantor stands poised to bridge worlds — weaving a
 coustic roots and futuristic soundscapes into a living web that invites li
 steners to move\, connect\, and transform.
LOCATION:HopMonk Tavern
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/1037644550?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=2
 87&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
