X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://raventheater.org/events/hisff-audience-favorites/", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/healdsburg-international-short-film-festival-audience-favorites/", "Press Democrat": "https://raventheater.org/events/hisff-audience-favorites/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://raventheater.org/events/hisff-audience-favorites/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Healdsburg International Short Film Festival Audience Favorites
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260411T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260411T153000
UID:260401uVcSDhkEPk2bduNwCWOiYg
DESCRIPTION:The Healdsburg International Short Film Festival showcases w
 ork from filmmakers of all ages and from all walks of life\, with represen
 tative work from as many as 50 countries. Available genres vary each year\
 , but always include narrative fiction\, documentaries\, and animation. Th
 e films in HISFF’s “Audience Favorites” represent the very best of
  the festival’s screenings from last September\, across all genres. Vol
 ume 1 will screen at 2 pm and 7:30 pm on Saturday\, April 11th and at 5 p
 m on Sunday\, April 12th. Volume 2 will screen at 5 pm on Saturday\, Apr
 il 11th and at 2 pm and 7:30 pm on Sunday\, April 12th. See both volumes t
 o (re)experience the HISFF 2025 audience’s favorite comedies\, dramas\, 
 documentaries\, and animation. Laugh\, cry\, and experience the beauty of 
 storytelling with short films.\n\nWatch the official HISFF Audience Favori
 tes trailer!\n\nAbout HISFF: Our panel of notable judges from the entertai
 nment industry makes the HISFF an attraction for new and veteran filmmaker
 s alike — people like Ed Begley\, Jr.\, Laraine Newman\, Tom Waits\, an
 d so many more. Several judges attended in 2025\, including actor Ed Begle
 y\, Jr.\, who made a book-signing appearance at the Raven as part of festi
 val events. More festival judges are expected to attend in 2026\; read ab
 out the judges on the Raven’s festival webpage.\n\n**April 11-12**\, **
 2026**\n\n**VOL 1: Saturday:** 2:00 pm\; 7:30 pm. **Sunday:** 5:00 pm. *
 *VOL 2: Saturday:** 5:00 pm\; **Sunday:** 2:00 pm\; 7:30 pm. \n\n**Adul
 ts**: $20 per screening block (multiple films per block)\n\n**Students:**
  $10 per screening block (multiple films per block)
LOCATION:The Raven Performing Arts Theater
URL:https://raventheater.org/events/hisff-audience-favorites/
X-SOURCE:Creative Sonoma, North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/juke-joint-jukebox/18409967/2026-04-11T14", "Press Democrat": "https://app.arts-people.com/index.php?show=316486"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/juke-joint-jukebox/18409967/2026-04-11T14"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Juke Joint Jukebox
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260411T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260411T160000
UID:2604011Pe3UXED60mBAQ-UspJ0zg
DESCRIPTION:Returning to Spreckels\, Juke Joint Jukebox is an electrifyin
 g educational cabaret that brings the legends to life — Ella Fitzgerald\
 , Ray Charles\, Dorothy Dandridge\, Harry Belafonte\, and more. Part conce
 rt\, part history lesson\, this high-octane journey celebrates the artists
  who shaped American music with powerhouse vocals\, storytelling\, and irr
 esistible rhythm.\n\nJuke Joint Jukebox features the vocal talents of Gar
 y Stanford Jr.\, Bradley Kynard\, Skylaer Palacios\, Sharon Griffith\, Sol
 ona Husband\, Julie Dormire and Leo Kimuyu. They are joined by pianist Vic
 tor Hall\, guitarist Greg Call\, and drummer Lance Lee.\n\nFilled with soa
 ring songs\, poignant storytelling and live music\, Juke Joint Jukebox is
  a special event not to be missed!
LOCATION:Spreckels Center for the Performing Arts
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/juke-joint-jukebox/1840
 9967/2026-04-11T14
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107860475?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=287&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Dan Perlman
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260411T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260411T000000
UID:2603113TPSImiyDES0rQcVK2USzQ
DESCRIPTION:Dan Perlman is a comedian\, writer\, and director from New Yor
 k City. He co-created\, wrote\, and starred in Showtime’s critically-acc
 laimed comedy series\, Flatbush Misdemeanors. Dan made his directorial deb
 ut in the Flatbush episode\, “boomerang\,” which Vulture praised for i
 ts “masterful direction.” Dan also wrote and directed the award-winnin
 g short films\, Cramming and Practice Space.\n\nDan first co-created the p
 rize-winning digital series of Flatbush\, which served as the foundation f
 or the Showtime show. Made on zero-budget\, the first installment became O
 scar-qualified after winning Grand Jury Awards in its film festival run.\n
 \nAs a stand-up\, Dan has been featured on Comedy Central and was named on
 e of the New Faces at the Montreal Just For Laughs Festival. His debut alb
 um\, Emergency Contact\, is a staple on SiriusXM. Dan is a regular at the 
 Comedy Cellar in NYC and headlines venues across the country. His writing 
 has also appeared in The New Yorker.
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
URL:https://www.bandsintown.com/e/107860475?app_id=pkvts0on0m&came_from=28
 7&utm_medium=api&utm_source=partner_api&utm_campaign=event
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/head-over-heels/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/head-over-heels/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Head Over Heels
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260411T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260411T161500
UID:250801aJy6mnoexkO6IrdoQ5fPOw
DESCRIPTION:**A Kingdom at Risk\, a Beat That Won’t Quit\, and Love That
  Rules All!**\n\n***“It’s a feel good riot from start to finish.“* 
 — Jay Darcy\, Mancunion Media Group** \n\n**Get ready for a wild\, laugh
 -out-loud adventure with *HEAD OVER HEELS*—the electrifying musical come
 dy from the creative forces behind Hedwig and the Angry Inch\, Avenue Q\, 
 and Spring Awakening! Nominated for *Outstanding New Broadway Musical* in 
 2019 and powered by the chart-topping hits of the legendary all-female roc
 k band The Go-Go’s\, this high-energy show features beloved anthems like
  “We Got the Beat\,” “Our Lips Are Sealed\,” “Vacation\,” “H
 eaven is a Place on Earth\,” and “Mad About You.”**\n\n**Join a spir
 ited royal family on a whirlwind quest to save their kingdom from doom—o
 nly to realize that the key to their future isn’t written in fate\, but 
 in their own hearts. Packed with irresistible music\, over-the-top comedy\
 , and a whole lot of love\, *HEAD OVER HEELS* is a dazzling\, feel-good sp
 ectacle that will have you dancing in your seat!**\n\nThursdays\, Fridays 
 & Saturdays @ 7:30pm\, Saturdays and Sundays at 2:00pm Run Time: Two hours
 \, 15 mins including intermission\n\nThursdays Adult $33Fri/Sat Eve Adult 
 $44.95\; Senior $38.95\; Under 18 $31.95Sat/Sun Matinee Adult $55.95\; Sen
 ior $48.95Value seating $37.95\\*All prices include fees(707) 523-4185**bo
 xoffice@6thstreetplayhouse.com**
LOCATION:6th Street Playhouse
URL:https://6thstreetplayhouse.com/shows/2025-26/head-over-heels/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
