DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260415T194500
UID:260405I3FAh3k260ySlGTkCmp17A
DESCRIPTION:Join NorCal Public Media for a special free screening featurin
 g a brand-new Ken Burns–produced documentary: Henry David Thoreau. This
  special event explores powerful and deeply connected themes drawn from th
 e life and philosophy of Thoreau: nonviolent resistance\, environmental st
 ewardship\, and civic responsibility.\n\nFollowing the screening\, stay fo
 r a panel discussion that brings Thoreau’s ideas into today’s world wi
 th journalist and activist Greg King - who is featured on NorCal’s Emmy 
 Award–winning series Climate California - plus Annie Creswell\, Execut
 ive Director of Stewards of the Coast and Redwoods\, and Gail Seymour\, sc
 ientist and environmental justice advocate.
LOCATION:Petaluma Library
URL:https://live-sonomacounty.pantheonsite.io/event/henry-david-thoreau-do
 cumentary-screening-norcal-public-media-108085
