X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Intro to Wheel Throwing: 04/17-05/22 2026 — Sebastopol Center Fo
 r the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20260417T000000
DTEND:20260418T000000
UID:e0abe97a8bc2ece97be659a5e9c68830@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Intro to Wheel Throwing: 04/17-05/22 2026\n\n  \n    \n      \
 n        \n          $250.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nFridays\, Apri
 l 17 - May 22\, 2026 (6 sessions)5pm - 7:30pm$205 + $45 clay feeMaximum 10
  studentsThere will be an initial demo on throwing and trimming\, and you 
 will also receive one-on-one guidance.The class will end with learning to 
 attach a handle to a cup and glazing the cup with your chosen colors.The i
 nstructor will clear glaze your pieces once they have been bisqued at the 
 studio.Come prepared to get messy and have fun!About the Instructor: James
  Thomson has been a ceramics studio facilitator with Sebastopol Center of 
 the Arts for over 5 years. He holds a BA from San Jose State University an
 d has taken classes with Laney Junior College\, Santa Rosa Junior College\
 , Richmond Art Center. He enjoys sharing his acquired skills with those wh
 o are interested in broadening their relationship with clay. James approac
