 onoma County’s fresh spring awakening—curling new leaves\, flowering q
 uince\, tulips\, ranunculus\, iris\, wild mustard\, and fruit trees just b
 eginning to show off. Think rain-washed color\, happy greens\, and those i
 rresistible pops of coral\, violet\, and yellow that make spring feel bran
 d new.Focus on building strong compositions using color\, texture\, light\
 , and form\, developed through wet washes\, controlled washes\, and textur
 al techniques. Guided discussions explore the essential elements of visual
  art to help you create expressive\, individual work.All materials provide
 d\, Space limited to 10 studentsDiscussion break 12:30pm. Please bring a b
 rown bag lunchAbout the Instructor: Lynn Zachreson studied art at the Univ
 ersity of Minnesota and San Jose State University—Painting\, Printmaking
 : BA Fine Art. She has experience teaching all ages: Watercolor painting s
 kills\, 30+ years\, Watercolor figure painting 20+ years\, and Fine Art Ba
 sics with Mixed Media 20+ years. Lynn enjoys spending her time painting\, 
 teaching\, long distance hiking\, and gardening. View Lynn’s art here: h
 ttps://lynnzachresonart.com/\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n        
       \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/spring-botanicals-in-watercol
 or
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
