ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://winecountry-media.s3.amazonaws.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/5/2026/03/16184252/626825995_1380979174068082_6580355386187639845_n.jpg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/petaluma-river-high-tide-upstream-paddle/17972590/2026-04-18T14"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Petaluma River High Tide Upstream Paddle
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260418T144500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260418T164500
UID:260129gJ-6_SIftkuUwQEyHcEnyg
DESCRIPTION:When the tide is high\, the Petaluma River opens into a quiete
 r\, greener world.\n\nJoin The Floathouse crew for a gentle\, guided paddl
 e upstream\, timed to higher tides that allow access beyond the downtown c
 hannel and into a tranquil tidal slough. With extra water beneath us\, we
 ’re able to glide into calm\, lush stretches of the river that are norma
 lly out of reach.\n\nThis unhurried paddle highlights the natural beauty o
 f the Petaluma River’s brackish\, tidal waterway. Watch for great egrets
 \, blue herons\, snowy egrets\, turtles basking along the banks\, and abun
 dant plant life. The calm water and peaceful surroundings create a deeply 
 grounding experience—many guests say they feel their stress melt away wi
 thin minutes.\n\nAlong the way\, knowledgeable guides share stories of the
  river’s ecology and human history\, offering insight into how this uppe
 r channel has shaped—and continues to shape—Petaluma. It’s a rare op
 portunity to experience how close wild nature lives to the heart of downto
 wn.\n\nBeginner-friendly. Sit-on-top kayaks and all gear provided.
LOCATION:The Floathouse Petaluma
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/petaluma-river-high-tid
 e-upstream-paddle/17972590/2026-04-18T14
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"The Big Easy": "https://bigeasypetaluma.com/event/945-after-butter-n-eggs-parade/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bigeasypetaluma
X-SOURCE:The Big Easy
X-SOURCE-URL:https://bigeasypetaluma.com/events/
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260418T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260418T170000
DTSTAMP:20260406T171834
CREATED:20260327T033420Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260403T192607Z
UID:10003112-1776524400-1776531600@bigeasypetaluma.com
SUMMARY:945 after Butter n Eggs Parade
DESCRIPTION:Meet 945—a band with alt-rock roots\, bold emotional voice\, and a live show that hits both heart and floor. Emerging from Sonoma County’s rock scene\, they merge the raw energy of 1990s/2000s alt rock with modern ideas and a hauntingly strong female lead vocal. \nLead singer (raised in Petaluma)\, Sophia’s voice is one of the band’s core charms—dynamic\, raw\, honest\, capable of whisper-quiet emotion and full-tilt rocker power. Backed by stellar instrumentation and songwriting that deals in real life\, 945 delivers originals and reinterpretations that stay with you. \nToday’s show will feel like you’re front-row for a band on the brink; fun\, powerful\, and unafraid to hold you. Rock favorites\, fresh originals\, and that kind of performance that echoes well past the set-end. \nWhy You’ve Gotta Be Here after the parade: \nAlt rock with soul—fierce\, real\, and moving \nA band already earning accolades (Best Rock Band for 2 years in a row and best lead vocals for 3 years in a row through Bohemian Magazine)
URL:https://bigeasypetaluma.com/event/945-after-butter-n-eggs-parade/
LOCATION:The Big Easy\, 128 American Alley\, Petaluma\, CA\, 94952\, United States
CATEGORIES:Alternative Rock
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://bigeasypetaluma.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/03/IMG_9743.jpeg
END:VEVENT
