SUMMARY:Abstract Collage Minis - Create a Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T150000
UID:260324BTMdwtttsE-kzuZ6xiW18A
DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nSunday\, April 19\, 2026 11:00 AM – 3:00 PM\n\nL
 ocation\n\nRoom 110\n\nExperience Level\n\nAll Levels\n\nEvent Categories:
  Drawing & Painting\, Workshops\n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n16\\+\n\nRegistration Cos
 t:\n\n$115\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n$10\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$125\n\
 nIn this workshop\, French-American collage artist Catherine Cruz guides y
 ou in creating a cohesive series of abstract collages on four wood panels\
 , exploring color\, line\, shape\, design principles\, and paper-mounting 
 techniques.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nIn this workshop\, French-American colla
 ge artist Catherine Cruz will teach you how to create a dynamic series of 
 abstract collages using elements such as color\, line and shape. You will 
 work on four small wood panels to compose a cohesive series. Working on se
 veral panels at once offers several advantages\, including greater creativ
 e momentum\, the ability to build a strong thematic connection between pie
 ces\, and a way to maintain creative flow. This technique allows for a dee
 per exploration of an idea or theme than is possible with a single piece. 
 We will start with short composition exercises to discuss design principle
 s and abstraction. Then Catherine will demonstrate her method for mounting
  papers on the panels. You will have ample time to select papers and creat
 e your designs. We will take a short break for lunch between 12:30 and 1:0
 0 pm so please bring your lunch and a beverage. What you’ll learn from t
 his workshop:\n\nReliable method for layering collage papers\n\nCreative w
 ays to explore abstraction\n\nTechniques for creating a cohesive series\n\
 nStrategies for refining your composition\n\nIMPORTANT: Each participant m
 ust purchase and bring four 6”x6” cradled wood panels to the workshop.
  Instructions for where to purchase your panels and how to prepare them wi
 ll be provided upon registration.\n\nInstructor will provide: a wide assor
 tment of painted and printed collage papers\, brushes\, acrylic medium\, s
 cissors\, rulers.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center
URL:https://sonomacommunitycenter.org/programs/abstract-collage-minis/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net", "Press Democrat": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "http://www.upstairsartgallery.net"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Art Exhibit: The Poetic Landscape
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T180000
UID:2603185NNGJLO2ik25EdNrA8aZ4w
DESCRIPTION:Date: FOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE  3/13/26\n\n**APRIL EXHIBIT: THE 
 POETIC LANDSCAPE**\n\nEXHIBIT DATES:  March 30  – April 26\, 2026\n\n*
 *RECEPTION: SATURDAY\, APRIL 4\, 2026\, 3-5 pm: Join us to meet KAREN MILL
 ER and PHYLLIS RAPP\;  celebrate the show and enjoy a poetry reading by f
 eatured guest\, Linda Loveland Reid\, gallery artist and published author.
   Be sure to take part in the Gallery’s free monthly drawing for a beau
 tiful work by a Gallery artist.  Refreshments will be served.**\n\nSonoma
  County artist\, **Karen Miller\,** presents **The Poetic Landscape\,** pa
 stel paintings that convey Miller’s personal experience in connecting wi
 th the intrinsic beauty of natural places. In these pieces\, color\, fluid
  shapes and rhythmic design combine to create an uplifting mood – a true
  poetic interlude.  Evoking a happy mood\, “Geyserville Sunflowers\,”
  turning to the sun by nature\, joyfully dance in its luminescence. By the
  river’s edge\, concentric reflections conjure a calm sense of wellbeing
  in “Fetch.”  The viewer feels welcomed by a warm embrace entering a 
 shaded secret spot in “September Trellis.”  Focused on local scenes\,
  these works truly hone in on the stunning landscape out our doors.  Mill
 er remarked “ As I contemplate the very real places of beauty surroundin
 g us\, I try to express my painterly response in hopes it will engender re
 cognition by the viewers.” \n\nMeet the artist: Miller will be hosting 
 the Gallery on March 30\, April 5 & 15 from 11am to 2:30 pm.\n\n The Stai
 rway Smallworks Showcase features **Phyllis Rapp’s Magic Moments\,** a c
 ollection of watercolors that create an atmosphere that is both introspect
 ive and magical.  Familiar domestic scenes are transformed as humans inte
 ract with animals and birds in floral settings.  In “Silent Watcher” 
 the red-headed young woman’s green eyes lock onto ours as she stares ahe
 ad\, flanked by her avian companion.  Experiencing these works is a like 
 taking a mini-step on the wild side\, an exciting and fun experience.\n\nM
 eet the artist: Rapp will be hosting the Gallery on March 30 and April 10 
 from 11am to 6 pm.\n\nAlso join us for **ART NITE HEALDSBURG**\, Thursday\
 , April 2\, 5 – 6 pm.  The theme for the 2026 kickoff event is Bouquets
  to Art.  ART NITE Healdsburg\, held the 1st Thursday of Every Month\, is
  a community event celebrating art and creativity with over 20 galleries p
 articipating.  ArtNiteHealdsburg.com.\n\nUpstairs Art Gallery\, 306 Cente
 r Street\, Healdsburg\, CA 95448. (707) 431-4214.: OPEN DAILY: 11am – 6 
 pm.    **www.upstairsart gallery.net** \n\nFor further information: Con
 tact: Beverly Bird\, Press Contact\, at bvdrio@sonic.net or 707-799-1490.
LOCATION:Upstairs Art Gallery
URL:http://www.upstairsartgallery.net
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://personalspace.space/exhibitions/glyph"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:GLYPH  - Art Exhibition
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T150000
UID:2603100YO7mrcnIku3Hp5YakE9WA
DESCRIPTION:Glyph will be on view through May 3. Personal Space is open Su
 ndays 11 a.m. to 3 p.m. and by appointment.\n\nBig news! Personal Space is
  back from our \\(much needed\\) hiatus. Join us next Sunday\, March 15 \
 \(2-5pm\\) for the opening of  Glyph. This is our first opening since Vil
 lage opened up next door\, and it’s sure to be a party!\n\nFeaturing thi
 rteen artists from the Bay Area and beyond\, Glyph embraces a liminal spac
 e which allows subconscious connections to reign and centers gut feeling a
 s a source of poetry\, mystery\, and magic. Collectively\, these artists d
 raw from an enigmatic lexicon of symbols\, favoring inscrutable familiarit
 y over anything known or quantified. This intuitive language manifests thr
 ough a varied approach to material translation that underscores\, and cele
 brates\, our innate ability to understand things deeply without having to 
 define them in words.\n\nGlyph features works by:\n\nSadie Buckner \n\nLu
 is Estrada \n\nRochele Gomez \n\nKainoa Gruspe \n\nLéonie Guyer \n\nK
 lea McKenna\n\nMitzi Pederson \n\nBen Peterson \n\nJ Pendleton\n\nRobert
  Smithson \n\nEmma Spertus \n\nHenna Vainio \n\nRichard Zimmerman \n\n
 See link for details and artist bios.
LOCATION:Personal Space
URL:https://personalspace.space/exhibitions/glyph
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
