DESCRIPTION:Cinnabar Theater presents The Christians by Lucas Hnath\n\nA p
 owerful\, thought-provoking drama about faith\, conviction\, and the cost 
 of standing by your beliefs.\n\nWhen a beloved megachurch pastor delivers 
 a sermon that challenges a core doctrine\, his congregation is thrown into
  turmoil. What follows is an intimate and gripping exploration of belief\,
  doubt\, leadership\, and community—inviting audiences to wrestle with b
 ig questions that linger long after the final moment on stage.\n\n• Warr
 en Theater\, Sonoma State University \\(Ives Hall\\)\, 1801 East Cotati Av
 e\, Rohnert Park\, CA 94928\n\n• April 10–26\, 2026\n\n• Fridays & S
 aturdays at 7:30 PM | Sundays at 2:00 PM\n\n• Special Talkback Post Show
 : Sunday\, April 19\n\nDirected by Nathan Cummings and featuring a stellar
  cast\, this minimalist\, emotionally resonant production is recommended f
 or mature audiences.\n\nTickets: cinnabartheater.org
LOCATION:Sonoma State University
URL:https://cinnabartheater.org/show/thechristians/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/2026-apjourn", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/slow-wildflower-journey/18329580/2026-04-19T14"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/2026-apjourn"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Slow Wildflower Journey
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260419T160000
UID:260315rsFlhnZmFE6cdoNPhsPQ4Q
DESCRIPTION:Do you enjoy a slow walk in a valley\, breezes\, wil
 dflowers\, the sounds of songbirds\, the taste of a Douglas Fir
  needle or a California Bay leaf\, the aroma of Tarweed\, or w
 atching wild turkeys and California Quail hunt for seeds and ins
 ects in the grass? Join Certified California Naturalists and Suga
 rloaf docents for this series of meandering Sunday afternoon expl
 orations. Each month (weather permitting) we will explore one or
  two of our accessible trails-- the Creekside Nature Trail\, and
  the Meadow Trail. Suitable for all levels and a range of mobi
 lity\, these Sunday afternoon adventures will accommodate people u
 sing walkers or wheelchairs\, young children\, parents with babies
  in strollers\, as well as those who just enjoy slow walks in
  nature that stimulate the five senses. Our April outing will f
 ocus on the wildflowers of Sugarloaf.\n\nTickets are $5 for adult
 s and free for children under 18 years of age (a parent or le
 gal guardian must accompany minors). Meet at the White Barn park
 ing lot. There will be frequent stops and opportunities for conv
 ersation\, photography\, nature journaling\, wildlife viewing\, rest
 ing\, etc.\, so bring your nature journal\, camera\, or binocular
 s if you have them. Wear comfortable shoes\, a hat\, sun protec
 tion\, bring water and if desired\, a snack. Parking fees apply.
  Rain cancel. In the event of rain\, we will reschedule to Sun
 day\, April 12\, at the same time.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/2026-apjourn
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
