SUMMARY:Free Training on Trauma-Informed Care and Workplace Wellbeing
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260421T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260421T170000
DTSTAMP:20260324T144131Z
UID:20260421T220000Z-17033@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260421T150000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,500,500/579_square_-_Career-Ed-Logo-Color-500x500_0.
 rev.1774389215.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:We are excited to share that the Social Work and Human Service
 s program is hosting a free training on Trauma-Informed Care and Workplace
  Wellbeing\, presented by Hanna Center\, for our SWHS students and the bro
 ader campus community!  Date: April 21st\, 2026  Time: 3:00–5:00 PM  Loc
 ation: SRJC Student Activity Center (SAC)  This 2-hour interactive session
  will explore the principles of Trauma-Informed Care and their application
  in professional environments. Participants will learn how to recognize an
 d respond to signs of burnout\, compassion fatigue\, and vicarious trauma 
 — and develop strategies to strengthen resilience and wellbeing.  This t
 raining is especially valuable for anyone in the helping professions or th
 ose looking to foster a more supportive\, trauma-informed workplace cultur
 e.  For more support\, visit SRJC's Human Services website. (https://human
 services.santarosa.edu/)
LAST-MODIFIED:20260324T215629Z
LOCATION:Bertolini Student Activity Center - Santa Rosa Campus
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/17033-free-training-on-trauma-inf
 ormed-care-and
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  We are excited to share that the Social 
 Work and Human Services program is hosting a free training on Trauma-Infor
 med Care and Workplace Wellbeing\, presented by Hanna Center\, for our SWH
 S students and the broader campus community!</p><p>  Date: April 21st\, 20
 26<br />  Time: 3:00–5:00 PM<br />  Location: SRJC Student Activity Cent
 er (SAC)</p><p>  This 2-hour interactive session will explore the principl
 es of Trauma-Informed Care and their application in professional environme
 nts. Participants will learn how to recognize and respond to signs of burn
 out\, compassion fatigue\, and vicarious trauma — and develop strategies
  to strengthen resilience and wellbeing.</p><p>  This training is especial
 ly valuable for anyone in the helping professions or those looking to fost
 er a more supportive\, trauma-informed workplace culture.</p><p>  For more
  support\, <a href="https://humanservices.santarosa.edu/" target="_blank" 
 rel="noopener">visit SRJC's Human Services website.</a></p>
X-LIVEWHALE-ID:17033
