DESCRIPTION:Schedule\n\nWednesdays\, April 1 – May 6\, 2026 1:30 PM – 
 4:30 PM\n\nLocation\n\nRoom 117\, Ceramics Studio\n\nExperience Level\n\nI
 ntermediate and Advanced\n\nEvent Categories: Ceramics\, Extended Classes\
 n\nAge\\(s\\)\n\n17\\+\n\nRegistration Cost:\n\n$200\n\nMaterials Fee:\n\n
 $30\n\nTotal Registration Cost:\n\n$230\n\nLevel up your personal practice
  with is Special Projects course focused on bringing your own vision to li
 fe with support from an instructor.\n\nAbout the Class\n\nThis course is d
 esigned for students already enrolled in at least one other class or who h
 ave an active personal studio practice and are seeking more guided\, one o
 n one time with an instructor. In this course\, students are expected to c
 ome with a project in mind\, and Instructor Lynn Wood will support each st
 udent with individualized techniques and skill learning. Lynn Wood has yea
 rs of experience in hand building\, and in this course\, she generously sh
 ares her problem solving skills with her students.\n\nGet 20% off when you
  sign up for both Handbuilding workshops\n\nIf you register for Dive Deepe
 r as well as Handbuilt Pots you can receive 20% off your total registratio
 n cost. Both classes are on the same day and run April 1 – May 6. There 
 will be a 30 minute break between sessions. You can call the front desk at
  \\(707\\) 938-4626 or email sean@sonomacommunitycenter.org to receive the
  discount.
