X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/emergence-spring-through-the-eyes-of-the-artists/", "Press Democrat": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/emergence-spring-through-the-eyes-of-the-artists/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/emergence-spring-through-the-eyes-of-the-artists/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Emergence - Spring Through the Eyes of the Artists
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T160000
UID:260401wlr04CLf3kuFhm5mkztS8w
DESCRIPTION:"Emergence" brings together the Artists of Fulton Crossing to 
 explore what Spring means to their creative lives. Spring is more than a s
 eason. It's a metaphor. It's renewal\, risk\, color\, thawing\, blooming\,
  awakening\, and sometimes even struggles. The public is invited to enjoy 
 this free Art exhibit and to take time to wander through the artists studi
 os and gallery spaces. Meet the artists at our opening reception March 21s
 t. Upcoming Art Workshops: March 21: Painting Easter Cookies. April 18: Ci
 gar Box Collage. May 16: Succulent Garden Centerpiece. Make treasures to b
 ring home. All ages welcome. Materials provided. E-mail Brenda at nanaspre
 ttypaper@outlook.com for preregistration and workshop info.
URL:https://creativesonoma.org/event/emergence-spring-through-the-eyes-of-
 the-artists/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/we-the-sculptors-international-sculpture-days/18433856/2026-04-25T11", "Creative Sonoma": "https://creativesonoma.org/event/we-the-sculptors-international-sculpture-days/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.pressdemocrat.com/events/#/details/we-the-sculptors-international-sculpture-days/18433856/2026-04-25T11"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/we-the-sculptors-international-sculpture-days/18433856/2026-04-25T11"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:"We The Sculptors…International Sculpture Days
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T160000
UID:260331Zmvc7kVi00mPOazXeHL4hw
DESCRIPTION:From ancient monuments carved in stone to bold contemporary ab
 straction\, sculpture has always been a defiant presence in the world. It 
 occupies space and refuses to be ignored.\n\nThis year’s International S
 culpture Days event embraces the belief that sculpture can inspire\, provo
 ke\, and challenge the world around us. Each artist will present their wor
 k \, and visitors can engage in acts of “defiant dissidence\,” explori
 ng how art can serve as both personal reflection and public voice.\n\nThe 
 event draws on a long tradition of artists and citizens using visual langu
 age to express dissent\, question norms\, and imagine new possibilities. A
 t its core\, *We The Sculptors* affirms the enduring role of artists to ch
 allenge\, to question\, and to stand visibly in the public square.
LOCATION:T Barny Gallery & Sculpture Garden
URL:https://bohemian.com/events-calendar/#/details/we-the-sculptors-intern
 ational-sculpture-days/18433856/2026-04-25T11
X-SOURCE:Creative Sonoma, North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://lomavistafarm.org/spring-open-house-is-almost-here/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Loma Vista Farm Spring Open House
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T150000
UID:260325HT5CzYp7DEG5wTsaxp86Yw
DESCRIPTION:We’re opening The Farm to the community for our first big ev
 ent of 2026.\n\nOur annual Spring festival is a grand showcase of our hors
 es\, alpacas\, pigs\, ducks\, chickens\, rabbits\, and more. It’s the fi
 rst opportunity for our supporters and the community to tour the farm and 
 meet the animals.\n\nLast year we finished building the chicken coop\, the
  cow barn\, and many other projects. We’ll be tidying up and getting rea
 dy for the big event over the next.\n\nA small fee may apply for some ente
 rtainment and activities.\n\nPlant Sale. Stop by to see the chickens enjoy
 ing their new home!\n\nSustainable Solano food forest tour stop!\n\nIn par
 tnership with Vallejo City Unified School District .\n\nFree admission and
  parking.
LOCATION:Loma Vista Farm
URL:https://lomavistafarm.org/spring-open-house-is-almost-here/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/small-wonders-2/", "Press Democrat": "https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/small-wonders-2/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/small-wonders-2/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Small Wonders
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260425T170000
UID:260324gGbti2J3PEKl2mBCULhPWA
DESCRIPTION:Call for Art: Small Wonders\n\nSome of the most exquisite beau
 ty can be captured in the smallest of images and objects: the iridescence 
 of a hummingbird in flight\, a millefiori paperweight\, Faberge eggs\, or 
 a miniature woven basket. These pieces are modest in size but powerful in 
 creativity and expression.\n\nHealdsburg Center for the Arts (HCA) invites
  artists to submit paintings\, original fine art prints\, collage\, mixed 
 media\, drawings\, fiber arts\, sculptures\, ceramics\, and jewelry for th
 is exhibition.\n\nApplication Requirements:\n\n\\- Platform: All applicati
 ons must be submitted via EntryThingy\n\n\\- Eligibility: Work must be ori
 ginal and completed within the past two years. Photos in the application m
 ust represent the actual work intended for exhibition.\n\n\\- Size/Weight:
  Artwork must not exceed 12" x 12" unframed (144 sq in) or 196 sq in frame
 d. Maximum weight is 40 lbs.\n\n\\- Display: 2-D pieces must be securely w
 ired (no alligator clips). 3-D work must be stable\; artists are responsib
 le for on-site assembly if required.\n\n\\- Sales: All work must be for sa
 le. HCA retains a 40% commission\; artists receive 60%. Please list retail
  prices only.\n\nKey Dates:\n\n\\- Entry Deadline: May 10\, 2026 (9 PM)\n\
 n\\- Notification of Selection: By May 13\, 2026\n\n\\- Shipped Work Deadl
 ine: Wednesday\, May 27\, 2026 (must include pre-paid return label)\n\n\\-
  Hand-Delivery: Sunday\, May 31 (12–4 PM) and Monday\, June 1 (11 AM–1
  PM)\n\n\\- Exhibition Dates: June 4\, 2026 – July 19\, 2026\n\n\\- Open
 ing Reception: Saturday\, June 6\, 2026 (4–6 PM)\n\n\\- Pick-up/Return S
 hipping: July 19 (12–4 PM) and July 20 (11 AM–1 PM)\; shipping the wee
 k of July 20.\n\nEntry Fees:\n\n\\- Non-Members: $50 (1 entry)\, $55 (2 en
 tries)\, $60 (3 entries). Includes a $60 yearly supporter membership.\n\n\
 \- Current Members: $40 (1 entry)\, $45 (2 entries)\, $50 (3 entries).
LOCATION:Healdsburg Center for the Arts
URL:https://healdsburgcenterforthearts.org/small-wonders-2/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
