SUMMARY:Deep Sky Astrophotography Image Capture (class 3 of 3)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T203000
DTSTAMP:20260407T031337Z
UID:cpnedhgf5gmhfvqse9bohum0v4@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260430T183000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20251010T213045Z
DESCRIPTION:<p>Do you understand the fundamentals of deep sky image proces
 sing\, and would you now like to learn how to capture your own raw data? 
  This class is for you!<br><br>Note that this class is designed for stude
 nts who have already attended the RFO “Deep Sky Astrophotography Process
 ing Class” or for students who already have experience with basic astrop
 hotography image processing.<br><br>What you will learn in this class:<br>
 -    A refresher on the fundamentals of Deep Sky Astrophotography<br>- 
    A review of the equipment and techniques required for deep sky image 
 capture <br>-    Hands-on experience capturing deep sky images at the Ro
 bert Ferguson Observatory<br>-    An opportunity to discuss techniques\,
  share images and get feedback from docents and fellow students<br><strong
 ><br></strong></p><p><strong>Please note\, this workshop is meant as a 3-c
 lass series. It is highly recommended to purchase tickets for all three da
 ys.</strong><br></p><p><strong>Please note\, class 1 and 3 are virtual. A 
 Zoom link will be sent to participants prior to the class.</strong> <b>Cl
 ass 2 will be in person at the Robert Ferguson Observatory. </b></p><p>Ge
 t more information and purchase tickets at <a href="https://www.google.com
 /url?q=http://rfo.simpletix.com&amp\;sa=D&amp\;source=calendar&amp\;ust=17
 37563198376784&amp\;usg=AOvVaw3MILLYGqpqAbL6ibtROWhJ" target="_blank">rfo.
 simpletix.com</a>.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20251010T213045Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
X-SOURCE:Robert Ferguson Observatory
X-SOURCE-URL:https://rfo.org/index.php/calendar-of-events/
