SUMMARY:Summer Solstice Soirée
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T203000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T223000
DTSTAMP:20260407T031337Z
UID:2eg3kbt335h585vkqtrhohvbqg@google.com
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260620T203000
SEQUENCE:0
CREATED:20251125T232812Z
DESCRIPTION:<p><i>Celebrate the longest day—and brightest night—of the
  year!</i></p><p>Welcome summer with an unforgettable evening under the st
 ars at the <b>Robert Ferguson Observatory’s Summer Solstice Soirée</b>
 ! Join us as we celebrate the turning of the season with good company\, tw
 ilight views of the Sonoma hills\, and a night of celestial discovery.</p>
 <p>As the sun sets on the longest day of the year\, enjoy summertime treat
 s and the warm glow of golden hour at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park. Once dar
 kness falls\, our observatory telescopes will open for guided viewing of t
 he night sky—featuring planets\, star clusters\, and deep-sky wonders. O
 ur astronomers and docents will be on hand to share insights about the sol
 stice\, the science behind it\, and its significance across cultures.</p><
 p>Come for the sunset\, stay for the starlight\, and celebrate the beauty 
 of our shared skies.</p><p>Space is limited ~ register at <a href="http://
 rfo.simpletix.com">rfo.simpletix.com</a>.</p>
LAST-MODIFIED:20251125T232813Z
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-SOURCE:Robert Ferguson Observatory
X-SOURCE-URL:https://rfo.org/index.php/calendar-of-events/
END:VEVENT
